WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.152
Time passed, and it was soon spring.

2
00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:12.830
The air grew warm, flowers bloomed, and birds swooped from tree to tree.

3
00:00:12.831 --> 00:00:18.847
The road Wukong and the others were traveling began to go up a mountain.

4
00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:21.178
[g@Wukong stopped the group.

5
00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:23.977
"Bajie, go up the road and search the mountain.@g]

6
00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:27.888
There might be a demon up there, and I don't want Master to get hurt."

7
00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:30.406
[g@"Ugh," moaned the pig.

8
00:00:30.407 --> 00:00:33.631
"You make me do all the hard work."@g]

9
00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:37.887
Dragging his feet, he headed up the mountain road.

10
00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:41.198
[g@Wukong turned to the Tang Monk and Wujing.

11
00:00:41.199 --> 00:00:43.057
"I'm going to follow the pig.@g]

12
00:00:43.058 --> 00:00:47.889
I want to make sure he really searches the mountain."

13
00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:57.682
The monkey turned invisible and followed Bajie up the road.

14
00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:00.797
The pig walked for a few minutes.

15
00:01:00.798 --> 00:01:05.379
When he was sure his companions wouldn't hear him, he turned around.

16
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.032
"You dummies!" shouted Bajie.

17
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.397
[g@"You make me do all the hard work!

18
00:01:10.398 --> 00:01:11.643
Well, guess what?@g]

19
00:01:11.644 --> 00:01:14.408
[g@I'm not going to search this mountain.

20
00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:17.389
I'm going to take a nap instead.@g]

21
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.879
And when I come back, I'll lie and say I searched the mountain!"

22
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:34.495
[g@Bajie found a big log.

23
00:01:34.496 --> 00:01:42.088
He lay down behind it and fell fast asleep.@g]

24
00:01:42.089 --> 00:01:45.470
[g@"This pig is so lazy," thought Wukong.

25
00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.337
"I'll teach him a lesson."@g]

26
00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:51.762
The monkey turned himself into a woodpecker and pecked the log.

27
00:01:51.763 --> 00:01:57.086
[i@Tap, tap, tap! Tap, tap, tap!@i]

28
00:01:57.087 --> 00:02:00.017
Bajie rolled over and mumbled.

29
00:02:00.018 --> 00:02:02.154
[g@Wukong pecked again.

30
00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:06.296
[i@Tap, tap, tap! Tap, tap, tap!@i]@g]

31
00:02:06.297 --> 00:02:07.928
[g@The pig sat up.

32
00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:10.507
"Quit tapping, you annoying woodpecker!@g]

33
00:02:10.508 --> 00:02:13.091
[g@I'm trying to sleep!"

34
00:02:13.092 --> 00:02:16.534
He fell asleep again.@g]

35
00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:19.004
[g@Wukong landed on Bajie's head.

36
00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.058
[i@Tap, tap, tap! Tap, tap, tap!@i]@g]

37
00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:26.669
"Ouch!" cried the pig, jumping to his feet.

38
00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.887
Wukong flew away.

39
00:02:28.888 --> 00:02:30.716
[g@Bajie rubbed his head.

40
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:35.233
"I can't even take a nap!"@g]

41
00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:40.327
He sighed. "I guess I'll go back down."

42
00:02:40.328 --> 00:02:44.259
When Bajie found his companions, he lied.

43
00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.726
"I searched the entire mountain," he said. "It's safe."

44
00:02:49.727 --> 00:02:53.887
"Did you see any demons or monsters?" asked Wukong.

45
00:02:53.888 --> 00:02:56.817
Bajie shook his head.

46
00:02:56.818 --> 00:03:00.624
[g@"How about woodpeckers?" asked the monkey.

47
00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:03.080
"Did you see any of them?"@g]

48
00:03:03.081 --> 00:03:04.997
[g@The pig looked surprised.

49
00:03:04.998 --> 00:03:07.740
"What . . . how did you . . . ?"@g]

50
00:03:07.741 --> 00:03:11.289
"That was me, Bajie!" shouted Wukong.

51
00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.170
[g@"You took a nap!

52
00:03:13.171 --> 00:03:16.493
You didn't search the mountain at all!"@g]

53
00:03:16.494 --> 00:03:18.611
Bajie hung his head.

54
00:03:18.612 --> 00:03:23.465
"You should be ashamed of yourself, Bajie," said Wujing.

55
00:03:23.466 --> 00:03:25.913
[g@The Tang Monk frowned.

56
00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:28.713
"Please go back and search the mountain, Bajie."@g]

57
00:03:28.714 --> 00:03:36.568
The pig headed back up the road.

58
00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:41.416
He had walked for a while when he saw a fox.

59
00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:44.756
"I know that's you, Wukong!" he shouted.

60
00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.592
[g@He swung his rake.

61
00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:49.030
The fox trotted away.@g]

62
00:03:49.031 --> 00:03:53.128
A robin flew past Bajie's head.

63
00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:56.808
"Get away from me, Wukong!" yelled the pig.

64
00:03:56.809 --> 00:04:02.180
As he waved the rake at the bird, Bajie tripped and fell.

65
00:04:02.181 --> 00:04:04.517
"Wukong!" shouted the pig.

66
00:04:04.518 --> 00:04:06.568
[g@"I know you're here.

67
00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:09.769
You're invisible, and you just tripped me."@g]

68
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.474
He got back up and stood still for a moment.

69
00:04:13.475 --> 00:04:20.063
When he didn't see or hear Wukong, he continued walking.

70
00:04:20.064 --> 00:04:29.725
Every time Bajie saw an animal, he waved his rake and yelled.

71
00:04:29.726 --> 00:04:32.776
[g@The road became very steep.

72
00:04:32.777 --> 00:04:35.369
The pig soon came to a cave.@g]

73
00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:39.983
In front of the cave was a demon.

74
00:04:39.984 --> 00:04:42.158
[g@Bajie held out his rake.

75
00:04:42.159 --> 00:04:45.119
"Tell me who you are!" he demanded.@g]

76
00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.111
[g@"My name is Golden Horn," said the demon.

77
00:04:49.112 --> 00:04:51.262
"Who are you?"@g]

78
00:04:51.263 --> 00:04:54.371
"I am Zhu Bajie," said the pig.

79
00:04:54.372 --> 00:04:58.144
"I'm traveling to the Western Paradise with the Tang Monk."

80
00:04:58.145 --> 00:05:01.230
[g@"Oh, the Tang Monk . . ."

81
00:05:01.231 --> 00:05:04.900
A smile curled along the demon's lips.@g]

82
00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:16.331
"I have heard that anyone who eats the Tang Monk will live forever."

